    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pick\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIf I open `MiniPick.builtin.files()` and choose a file with a name containing an HH:MM timestamp, such as `Feb_16_2024_10:40_PM.py`, the file is not opened.\r\n\r\nThe issue appears to be in `parse_path` in `mini/pick.lua`. This function has some special handling for paths containing patterns like `:10:5` that's being tripped up by timestamps.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.5\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Create a file named `Feb_16_2024_10:40_PM.py`\r\n2. Open nvim and call `MiniPick.builtin.files()`\r\n3. Choose `Feb_16_2024_10:40_PM.py`\r\n4. Note that the file is not opened\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe selected file should be opened.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThe selected file is not opened.",
