            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Maybe somewhat surprisingly, but right now I think that the best course of action would be to say \"Avoid using semicolons in file names\" (which is a good advice in general, to be honest).\r\n\r\nGenerally I’d agree, but I didn’t name these files 😄\r\n\r\nMaybe `parse_path`, or something higher in the chain, could check to see whether the path actually exists as a file and therefore doesn’t need to be parsed.",
