        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hmm…true, that would be expensive.\r\n\r\nMaybe the picker could just take an option that could indicate that the items are simple paths? Like `MiniPick.builtin.files({ process_paths=false })`? It might be generally useful to be able to tell the file picker that it’s only working with file paths, and that it shouldn’t try to interpret the paths as anything else.",
