        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Hmm…true, that would be expensive.\r\n> \r\n> Maybe the picker could just take an option that could indicate that the items are simple paths? Like `MiniPick.builtin.files({ process_paths=false })`? It might be generally useful to be able to tell the file picker that it’s only working with file paths, and that it shouldn’t try to interpret the paths as anything else.\r\n\r\nIt is not so much about the picker itself (as `builtin.files()` indeed always works with plain file paths), but more about `default_choose()` and some other helpers (which are written for a wider tasks). I'll look into it.",
