        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks again for the issue!\r\n\r\nI could not find a non-breaking after several attempts, so decided to go ahead and make a slightly breaking change. Now having `{ path = 'file:1:2' }` as an item will be recognized as file by `default_preview()`, `default_choose()`, and `default_choose_marked()` (previously they were still trying to parse this as `path:line:col` format).\r\n\r\nThis allowed modifying `builtin.files()` to use this table format only for paths which contain \":\", making them work without much overhead. So this should be fixed on latest `main`.",
            "created_at": "2024-04-09T17:07:59Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/714#issuecomment-2045704260",
